course: dictionary
lesson: 6959
title: Palindromes: words that read both ways
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A palindrome is a word, number or sentence that reads the same backwards as forwards. Say «level» aloud, then spell it backwards: l-e-v-e-l. It is the same both ways, so level is a palindrome.
explain: Other examples are «noon», «mum», «Nan» and «racecar», and numbers such as «12321». When you check a sentence, ignore the spaces, capitals and punctuation. «Was it a car or a cat I saw?» is a palindrome sentence.
explain: Palindromic is the adjective, so you can talk about «palindromic numbers» such as 121 or 4004. Names like Anna and Otto are palindromes too.
fact: A palindrome reads the same forwards and backwards.
fact: Palindrome words include «mum», «noon», «kayak» and «civic».
fact: In a sentence, ignore spaces, capitals and punctuation: «Was it a car or a cat I saw?» is a palindrome.
fact: A palindromic number reads the same both ways, such as 121 or 12321.
fact: Puzzle: reverse a number and add it to itself. 56 + 65 = 121, which is a palindrome.
exercise: Which of these is a palindrome? | green | *noon | apple | table
exercise: Why is 121 a palindromic number? | *It reads 121 both ways | It is an odd number, so it cannot be a palindrome | No, because it has three digits | It is bigger than 100
exercise: Which sentence is a palindrome if you ignore spaces, capitals and punctuation? | Good morning, class. | I went home today. | *«Was it a car or a cat I saw?» | The cat sat on the mat.
test: Which name is a palindrome? | Tom | Ben | *Anna | Chloe
test: In the puzzle 56 + 65 = 121, what is the answer? | 1212 | 65 only | 56, because nothing changes | *121, which is a palindrome
exam: Sam says «kayak» is not a palindrome because it has five letters. Is Sam right? | Yes, because kayak is a type of boat | No, because kayak has a letter y in it | *No, k-a-y-a-k reads the same both ways, so it is a palindrome | Yes, words with five letters can never be palindromes
